WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.000
God’s name Jehovah means “I AM.”

00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:08.000
“I AM” is like a blank for us to fill through experience.

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:15.000
This God has many aspects that we can experience.

00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:21.000
This afternoon at my mother’s memorial, a sister mentioned a hymn.

00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:27.000
I had taught my mother this hymn, and she loved it.

00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:34.000
The hymn speaks of the many aspects of Christ we can experience.

00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:39.000
The hymn names forty-seven aspects.

00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:51.000
We can experience every one of them for ourselves.

00:00:57.000 --> 00:01:02.000
Let us look at Psalm 23.

00:01:02.000 --> 00:01:09.000
“Jehovah is my Shepherd.”

00:01:09.000 --> 00:01:17.000
Jehovah is the “I AM.” With Him as my Shepherd, I shall not want.

00:01:17.000 --> 00:01:24.000
He is everything, the Alpha and the Omega.

00:01:24.000 --> 00:01:30.000
He is the reality of all things.

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:36.000
If we know Him only objectively and do not experience Him, we remain poor.

00:01:38.000 --> 00:01:44.000
He makes me lie down in green pastures and leads me beside waters of rest.

00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:52.000
Though this psalm has only six verses, it contains a profound change.

00:01:52.000 --> 00:02:00.000
A sheep lies down in green pastures only after it has eaten its fill.

00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:08.000
If it is still hungry, it will keep eating when it sees grass.

00:02:08.000 --> 00:02:15.000
The sheep has also had its fill of water before resting beside it.

00:02:16.000 --> 00:02:23.000
God takes care of our physical needs.

00:02:23.000 --> 00:02:30.000
He also restores our soul.

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:36.000
Our soul is often confused and does not know which way to go.

00:02:36.000 --> 00:02:44.000
A brother who raises sheep told us that sheep have very poor eyesight.

00:02:44.000 --> 00:02:51.000
They cannot see clearly ahead, so they follow the sheep in front.

00:02:51.000 --> 00:02:57.000
If the sheep in front falls off a cliff, those behind may follow.

00:02:57.000 --> 00:03:00.000
That is why we need the Shepherd to lead us.
